# Explore SOUS — styling

Single source of tokens: **`src/app/globals.css`** (`@import "tailwindcss"`, `:root` variables, `@theme inline`, `@utility` typography). Framer reference: [explore-sous.framer.website](https://explore-sous.framer.website/) — design system routes under `/design-system/*` (e.g. [text-styles](https://explore-sous.framer.website/design-system/text-styles), [color-styles](https://explore-sous.framer.website/design-system/color-styles), [spacing](https://explore-sous.framer.website/design-system/spacing-system), [radius](https://explore-sous.framer.website/design-system/border-radius-system), [buttons](https://explore-sous.framer.website/design-system/buttons), [inputs](https://explore-sous.framer.website/design-system/input-fields), [modals](https://explore-sous.framer.website/design-system/modal-systen)).

## 1. Tailwind 4 patterns

- Prefer **utility classes**; avoid inline styles for color, spacing, radius, and typography.
- Use **semantic theme utilities** first: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, etc.
- Reach for **palette utilities** only when semantic tokens do not fit: `bg-ds-peach-600`, `text-ds-blue-900`, `bg-ds-blue-600`, `bg-ds-clay-100`.
- Merge conditional classes with **`cn()`** from **`@/lib/utils`**; forwarded components should accept **`className`** and merge last.

```tsx
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

<div
  className={cn(
    "base-classes",
    condition && "conditional-classes",
    className,
  )}
/>;
```

## 1b. shadcn / Radix primitives

- UI building blocks live in **`src/components/ui/`** (installed with **`npx shadcn@latest add <name>`**). Treat them as **owned source**: adjust with **`cn()`**, Framer tokens (`rounded-ds-*`, `type-h*-*`), and semantic colours—avoid parallel one-off components that duplicate the same behaviour.
- **Variants:** shadcn `button` and similar use **`class-variance-authority`** already; extend variants there instead of new wrapper components unless the UX diverges clearly.

## 2. Colour system (Framer → CSS → Tailwind)

Semantic mapping in `@theme inline` (use these first):

| Role | Utilities |
|------|-----------|
| Page surface | `bg-background`, `text-foreground` |
| Primary CTA / links accent | `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, hover `hover:bg-primary-hover` |
| Secondary / supporting text | `text-muted-foreground`, surfaces `bg-muted` |
| Hover surface (lists, fields, calendar cells) | `hover:bg-interactive-hover` (token: `--interactive-hover`) |
| Cards | `bg-card`, `text-card-foreground` |
| Borders / inputs outline | `border-border`, `border-input` |
| Focus ring | `ring-ring` (pair with `focus-visible:ring-2`) |
| Success / warning (badges, alerts) | `text-success`, `bg-success-muted`, `text-warning`, `bg-warning-muted` |
| Destructive | `bg-destructive`, `text-destructive-foreground` |

**Raw palette** (`bg-ds-*`, `text-ds-*`): `ds-blue-{600,900}`, `ds-peach-{50,100,600,800,900}`, `ds-green-{50,100,600,800,900}`, `ds-yellow-{50,100,600,800,900}`, `ds-clay-{50,100,200,600,800,900}`. **Alpha overlays:** use CSS vars in arbitrary values, e.g. `bg-[var(--ds-alpha-black-8)]`, until exposed as theme colors if needed.

**Do not** paste one-off hex colours in JSX—add or reuse a token in `globals.css` first.

Colour space is **hex from Framer** for fidelity; migrating key tokens to **OKLCH** later is fine if you keep the same names in `@theme`.

## 3. Typography (Framer text styles)

Framer names: **H1 Semibold** … **H6 Medium**. In code use **`@utility`** classes (rem-based, same proportions as Framer px):

| Utility | Framer analogue |
|---------|-----------------|
| `type-h1-sb` | H1 Semibold |
| `type-h2-sb` | H2 Semibold |
| `type-h2-md` | H2 Medium |
| `type-h3-sb` … `type-h6-md` | H3–H6 Semibold / Medium |
| `type-body-md` | Body Medium (16px / medium) |
| `type-body-sm-sb` | Body Small Semibold (14px / semibold) |

Body copy: default document styles use **`font-sans`** (**Inter** via `next/font`, variable `--font-inter`). OpenType flags live in **`--inter-features`** in `globals.css` (Framer parity). Use **`font-mono`** (Geist Mono) only for code.

## 4. Spacing (4px base)

Framer spacing system: **base unit 4px**. Prefer Tailwind spacing scale **`p-*`, `m-*`, `gap-*`, `space-*`** so rhythm stays **4px multiples** (e.g. `gap-2` = 8px, `gap-4` = 16px at default `spacing` scale). Avoid arbitrary pixel gaps unless they match that grid.

## 5. Border radius (Framer tokens)

| Framer token | Utility | Typical usage |
|--------------|---------|----------------|
| radius-4 | `rounded-ds-4` | Tiny badges, micro UI |
| radius-8 | `rounded-ds-8` | Cards, inputs, small controls |
| radius-10 | `rounded-ds-10` | **Primary buttons** (default; rare elsewhere) |
| radius-12 | `rounded-ds-12` | Dropdowns, tooltips, panels |
| radius-16 | `rounded-ds-16` | Modals, bottom sheets |
| radius-20 | `rounded-ds-20` | Feature cards, hero surfaces |
| radius-24 | `rounded-ds-24` | Large mobile surfaces (e.g. search bar) |
| radius-full | `rounded-ds-full` | Pills, chips |

**Homepage search (outer radius − 2px for hovers):** `--search-control-inner-radius` and `--search-field-hover-radius` live in **`globals.css`** with utilities **`rounded-search-inner`** and **`rounded-search-field-hover`**. Mark the bar with **`data-search-field-surface`**; mark mobile picker sheets with **`data-search-dropdown="sheet"`** so inner radii track popover (`ds-12`) vs sheet (`ds-16`).

## 6. Buttons (Framer system)

Documented variants: **Primary**, **Secondary**, **Destructive**, **Ghost**, **Link**. Behaviour standards:

- **Layout:** `inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-medium transition-colors` (adjust with design).
- **Shape:** default to **`rounded-ds-10`** for primary button surfaces unless a spec says otherwise.
- **States:** always **`hover:`**, **`focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2`**, **`disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50`**.
- **Icons:** keep icon + label aligned; prefer `size-*` for square icons (e.g. `size-4`) and `gap-2`.

## 7. Input fields (Framer system)

States in Framer: **Default**, **Filled**, **Default • Mobile**, **Filled** (mobile). Pattern:

- **Label** (visible, associated with control).
- **Control:** full width, **`rounded-ds-8`**, border `border-input`, background distinct from page when “filled”.
- **Description** line under control for helper copy.
- **Placeholder:** `placeholder:text-muted-foreground`.
- **Invalid:** `aria-invalid:border-destructive` or `aria-invalid:ring-destructive/30` when applicable.

## 8. Modals (Framer system)

Framer examples: section header vs open header, optional footer, primary action. Standards:

- **Surface:** `rounded-ds-16`, `bg-card`, `text-card-foreground`, `border-border`, sensible **`p-6`** or token-based padding.
- **Backdrop:** `DialogContent` / `SheetContent` default to full scrim (`scrimAboveNavbar`, tokens in `@/lib/modal-overlay`). Use `modalOverlayScrimClass` / `modalPanelScrimClass` only inside primitives — not at feature call sites.
- **Opt-out:** explore mega menu sheet only — `scrimAboveNavbar={false}` and `overlayClassName="top-[var(--site-navbar-height)]"`.
- **Focus:** trap focus and restore on close (library or manual); first focusable element receives focus on open.

## 9. Cards, lists, tables

- **Default card:** `bg-card text-card-foreground border border-border rounded-ds-8 shadow-sm` (tune shadow when design specifies).
- **Large / marketing card:** prefer **`rounded-ds-20`**.
- **Tables:** scroll container `overflow-x-auto`, header row visually distinct (`bg-muted` or `border-b`), maintain **row min-height** for tap targets on mobile.

## 10. Shadows & elevation

Until tokens are added to `globals.css`, use Tailwind **`shadow-sm` / `shadow-md`** sparingly for cards and hovers (`hover:shadow-md`). Prefer one elevation pattern per surface type.

## 11. Interactive & motion

- **Hover:** always define for clickable elements (`hover:bg-*`, `hover:text-*`, `hover:border-*`).
- **Active (optional):** subtle `active:scale-[0.98]` for buttons only if product agrees.
- **Transitions:** prefer narrow props, e.g. **`transition-[color,box-shadow,opacity]`**, over `transition-all` unless justified.

## 12. Dark mode

The site **stays on the light `:root` tokens** (no `prefers-color-scheme` flip in `globals.css`). **`html { color-scheme: light; }`** matches native UI to that theme. Optional **`.dark`** on `<html>` later would need explicit **`dark:`** utilities.

## 13. Responsive behaviour

- **Mobile-first:** base styles for small viewports, then **`sm:`**, **`md:`**, **`lg:`**, **`xl:`** as needed.
- Breakpoints follow **Tailwind defaults** unless overridden in config.
- Prefer **container / flex / grid** utilities; use **`@container`** only when a component truly needs container queries.

## 14. Data attributes & composition

- Prefer **`data-slot="…"`** on reusable primitives (`button`, `card`, `input` root) for styling hooks: `[&_[data-slot=icon]]:size-4`.
- Use **`data-state`** for open/closed, selected, etc., when using headless patterns.

## 15. Accessibility

- Visible **`:focus-visible`** styles on all interactive elements.
- Pair **`aria-invalid`** with border/ring treatment on inputs.
- Respect **colour contrast** against `background` / `card`; do not rely on colour alone for state.

## 16. Anti-patterns

- Random **`#RRGGBB`** in class strings → **theme / `ds-*` token**.
- **`w-4 h-4`** pairs → prefer **`size-4`**.
- **Missing** hover/focus/disabled on interactive UI.
- **Typography** as ad-hoc `text-[56px]` everywhere → use **`type-h*-`** utilities.

## 17. File layout (this repo)

- **Global CSS & tokens:** `src/app/globals.css` (includes `@import "tw-animate-css"` and `@import "shadcn/tailwind.css"`).
- **`cn()`:** `src/lib/utils.ts`
- **shadcn primitives:** `src/components/ui/`
- **Layout-only building blocks (e.g. carousels):** `src/components/` when shared across features
- **Listing rails / horizontal sliders:** do not show prev/next arrow controls below the `sm` breakpoint; rely on swipe/scroll on mobile (`max-sm:hidden` on the nav cluster in `listingRailHeaderClassNames`).
- **Homepage composition:** `src/features/homepage/`

## 18. When Framer changes

Update **`src/app/globals.css`** and this rule in the **same PR** when the Framer design system pages change, so Cursor and the build stay aligned.
